README-ERRMSG -- the error message file, and BASIC09's numbers==============================================================SYS/errmsg is the text `perr' and the shell print for an error number.Its format has no comment syntax: a line is either    NNN:MMM text            an entry, class and code     text                   a continuation of the entry above itso what follows is written here.The file is original.  The code numbers and their E$ names are standardOS-9; the descriptions were written for this collection and checkedagainst the OS-9 v2.4 Technical Reference Manual.BASIC09 numbers its own errors 10-80, and runb reports them in the same000:NNN form as the kernel.  43 is BASIC09's "Unknown procedure"; OS-9has no 43.  Codes above 80 are OS-9's alone, and 1-9 are unused by both.The two collide at 64, 65, 66 and 67, where OS-9 has math-libraryerrors; those entries give the OS-9 meaning first and BASIC09's after.Under os9exec, error text comes from a table inside the emulator, andthis file is not read.  On OS-9 it is what `perr' reads.The BASIC09 programs on this disk are bio, blackjack and wysetime.DOC/INDEX says how to run them.